"suggestion": "1. **Typography & Identity**: Replace the current sans-serif font with a high-quality pixel font (e.g., 'Press Start 2P' or 'Silkscreen') for all text to commit to the retro identity. 2. **Note Highway**: Populate the highway panel with a stylized 4-lane grid, a glowing hit line, and a few sample notes to demonstrate the game mechanic and fill the empty space. 3. **START Button**: Redesign the button to use hard-edged, blocky shapes and a solid or dithered fill instead of smooth gradients. Remove the inconsistent vertical stripes or replace them with a clean, repeating pixel pattern. 4. **Layout & Balance**: Rebalance the composition by moving the title/description block to the top-left to anchor the layout, or center the entire content block to create a more cohesive, symmetrical menu screen. 5. **Color System**: Establish a strict 3-4 color palette (e.g., deep purple background, cyan primary, pink secondary, white text) and apply it consistently to all elements to improve visual coherence."
}

